IMPORT prelude

-- Departmental Titles (Alteration) Act 1950 (Singapore) -- which old title of office is replaced by which new one in any written
-- law or other document (s 2 and the Schedule), how far the substitution reaches, and who may change the Schedule (s 3).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (footer: "version in force from 1/10/2026"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/DTAA1950.txt. The cover says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the Schedule is annotated with later notifications, the latest being S 704/2026 wef 01/10/2026 (also S 550/2022, S 570/2024 and
-- S 571/2024). THE SCHEDULE IS COLUMN-SHIFTED IN THE .txt DEPOSIT on its pages 7 and 8: on page 7 the item numbers 89 to 101 are
-- printed in a stack above the entries, and on page 8 the new titles sit up to two lines above their old titles. The entries there
-- were matched by ORDER OF APPEARANCE (13 old and 13 new titles on page 7; 12 and 12, counting 107A, on page 8), not by line position.
-- The item numbers 89 to 101 given below for page-7 entries are an inference from that order.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0262 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. What it decides for a member of the public is how to read an office named in an old law, licence, deed or
-- form. SCOPED to 27 of the Schedule's 116 entries (44 titles), chosen where the Schedule does something structurally
-- interesting (chains, a title split in two, near-miss spellings) or that a member of the public meets (prisons, customs, registries
-- of births, deaths and marriages, the Shariah Court, ministries). Not encoded: the other Schedule entries, which are each a single
-- one-step substitution of the same shape; the legislative history.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Departmental Titles (Alteration) Act 1950 -- titles`

-- The Schedule's two columns are "Old title or name of office" and "New title or name of office". One type holds both, because a new
-- title in one row is often an old title in another.
DECLARE Title IS ONE OF
    -- prisons (items 4-7, 16-19)
    `Gaoler`
    `Warder`
    `Chief Sub-warder`
    `Sub-warder`
    `Chief Officer`
    `Principal Officer`
    `Chief Warder`
    `Chief Rehabilitation Officer`
    `Principal Rehabilitation Officer`
    `Commissioner of Prisons`
    `Director of Prisons`
    -- customs (items 20-25)
    `Revenue Officer`
    `Revenue Officer, Senior Grade`
    `Higher Revenue Officer`
    `Customs Officer`
    `Senior Customs Officer`
    `Chief Customs Officer`
    `Assistant Superintendent of Customs and Excise`
    `Senior Superintendent of Customs and Excise`
    -- registries (items 27, 28, 44, 45)
    `Registrar of Births, Deaths and Marriages`
    `Registrar of Births and Deaths`
    `Registrar of Marriages`
    `Chief Kathi`
    `Registrar of Muslim Marriages`
    `Registrar of Muslim Marriages and President, Shariah Court`
    `President, Shariah Court`
    -- social welfare (items 12, 81)
    `Assistant Secretary for Social Welfare`
    `Assistant Director of Social Welfare`
    `Welfare Officer Grade VII or VIII`
    -- Criminal Investigation Department (items 83, 87, and the page-7 entry taken as item 93)
    `Head of Administration and Specialist Division, Criminal Investigation Department`
    `Head of Support and Services Division, Criminal Investigation Department`
    `Assistant Director CID (Support and Services), Criminal Investigation Department`
    `Assistant Director CID (Support & Services), Criminal Investigation Department`
    `Assistant Director CID (Investigation Support & Services), Criminal Investigation Department`
    -- judiciary and legislation (items 104, 106, 107A)
    `Parliamentary Counsel`
    `Chief Legislative Counsel`
    `Deputy Chief Executive, Judiciary Administration and Operations of the Supreme Court`
    `Deputy Chief Executive of the Supreme Court`
    `Deputy Chief Executive, Office of the Chief Justice`
    -- ministries (items 102, 110, 114)
    `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Information, Communications and the Arts`
    `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Communications and Information`
    `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Trade and Industry`
    `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Energy, Trade and Industry`
    -- not in the Schedule at all
    `Commissioner of Police`

§§ `2 and the Schedule -- one substitution`

-- s 2: "Where in any written law or in any other document the title or name of office mentioned in the first column of the Schedule
-- is used, there is to be substituted for that title or name of office the title or name of office mentioned opposite it in the second
-- column of the Schedule."
--
-- Schedule rows encoded: 4 Gaoler -> Chief Officer; 5 Warder -> Principal Officer; 6 Chief Sub-warder -> Chief Warder; 7 Sub-warder ->
-- Warder; 16 Commissioner of Prisons -> Director of Prisons; 18 Chief Officer -> Chief Rehabilitation Officer; 19 Principal Officer ->
-- Principal Rehabilitation Officer; 20 Senior Customs Officer -> Senior Superintendent of Customs and Excise; 22 Customs Officer ->
-- Assistant Superintendent of Customs and Excise; 23 Higher Revenue Officer -> Chief Customs Officer; 24 Revenue Officer, Senior Grade ->
-- Senior Customs Officer; 25 Revenue Officer -> Customs Officer; 27 Registrar of Births, Deaths and Marriages -> Registrar of Births
-- and Deaths; 28 Registrar of Births, Deaths and Marriages -> Registrar of Marriages; 44 Registrar of Muslim Marriages and President,
-- Shariah Court -> President, Shariah Court; 45 Chief Kathi -> Registrar of Muslim Marriages; 12 Assistant Secretary for Social
-- Welfare -> Assistant Director of Social Welfare; 81 Assistant Director of Social Welfare -> Welfare Officer Grade VII or VIII; 83, 87
-- and (by order) 93 as named; 102 and 110 -> Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Digital Development and Information; 104 Parliamentary
-- Counsel -> Chief Legislative Counsel; 106 -> Deputy Chief Executive of the Supreme Court; 107A Deputy Chief Executive of the Supreme
-- Court -> Deputy Chief Executive, Office of the Chief Justice; 114 -> Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Energy, Trade and Industry.
--
-- Items 27 and 28 give the SAME old title twice with two different new titles. The Act does not say which applies where; this
-- function leaves that title unchanged, and `s 2 substitutes` below records both.
GIVEN `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A Title
DECIDE `the title after one substitution` IS
    CONSIDER `the title`
    WHEN `Gaoler` THEN `Chief Officer`
    WHEN `Warder` THEN `Principal Officer`
    WHEN `Chief Sub-warder` THEN `Chief Warder`
    WHEN `Sub-warder` THEN `Warder`
    WHEN `Commissioner of Prisons` THEN `Director of Prisons`
    WHEN `Chief Officer` THEN `Chief Rehabilitation Officer`
    WHEN `Principal Officer` THEN `Principal Rehabilitation Officer`
    WHEN `Senior Customs Officer` THEN `Senior Superintendent of Customs and Excise`
    WHEN `Customs Officer` THEN `Assistant Superintendent of Customs and Excise`
    WHEN `Higher Revenue Officer` THEN `Chief Customs Officer`
    WHEN `Revenue Officer, Senior Grade` THEN `Senior Customs Officer`
    WHEN `Revenue Officer` THEN `Customs Officer`
    WHEN `Registrar of Muslim Marriages and President, Shariah Court` THEN `President, Shariah Court`
    WHEN `Chief Kathi` THEN `Registrar of Muslim Marriages`
    WHEN `Assistant Secretary for Social Welfare` THEN `Assistant Director of Social Welfare`
    WHEN `Assistant Director of Social Welfare` THEN `Welfare Officer Grade VII or VIII`
    WHEN `Head of Administration and Specialist Division, Criminal Investigation Department`
        THEN `Head of Support and Services Division, Criminal Investigation Department`
    WHEN `Head of Support and Services Division, Criminal Investigation Department`
        THEN `Assistant Director CID (Support and Services), Criminal Investigation Department`
    WHEN `Assistant Director CID (Support & Services), Criminal Investigation Department`
        THEN `Assistant Director CID (Investigation Support & Services), Criminal Investigation Department`
    WHEN `Parliamentary Counsel` THEN `Chief Legislative Counsel`
    WHEN `Deputy Chief Executive, Judiciary Administration and Operations of the Supreme Court`
        THEN `Deputy Chief Executive of the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Deputy Chief Executive of the Supreme Court` THEN `Deputy Chief Executive, Office of the Chief Justice`
    WHEN `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Information, Communications and the Arts`
        THEN `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    WHEN `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Communications and Information`
        THEN `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    WHEN `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Trade and Industry` THEN `Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Energy, Trade and Industry`
    OTHERWISE `the title`

-- Whether the title appears in the first column at all.
GIVEN `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an old title in the Schedule` IF
        `the title` EQUALS `Registrar of Births, Deaths and Marriages`
    OR  (NOT (`the title after one substitution` `the title` EQUALS `the title`))

-- The relation s 2 sets up between an old and a new title. For items 27 and 28 it holds for both new titles.
GIVEN `the old title` IS A Title, `the new title` IS A Title
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2 substitutes` IF
    IF `the old title` EQUALS `Registrar of Births, Deaths and Marriages`
    THEN     `the new title` EQUALS `Registrar of Births and Deaths`
         OR  `the new title` EQUALS `Registrar of Marriages`
    ELSE     `is an old title in the Schedule` `the old title`
         AND `the new title` EQUALS `the title after one substitution` `the old title`

§§ `2 and the Schedule -- chains`

-- A new title in one row is the old title of another: Sub-warder -> Warder (item 7) -> Principal Officer (item 5) -> Principal
-- Rehabilitation Officer (item 19); Revenue Officer -> Customs Officer (25) -> Assistant Superintendent of Customs and Excise (22).
-- s 2 does not say whether the substitution is made once or repeated on its own result. INTERPRETIVE FORK, not resolved here:
-- `the title after one substitution` is the single pass; `the title after every substitution` repeats it until the title is no longer
-- in the first column. (Inference: the repeated reading is what a reader who applied s 2 to an already-substituted text would get.)
-- The Schedule has no cycle among the encoded titles, so the repetition ends.
GIVEN `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A Title
DECIDE `the title after every substitution` IS
    IF `the title after one substitution` `the title` EQUALS `the title`
    THEN `the title`
    ELSE `the title after every substitution` (`the title after one substitution` `the title`)

-- How many substitutions the chain takes.
GIVEN `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the length of the chain from` IS
    IF `the title after one substitution` `the title` EQUALS `the title`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 1 + `the length of the chain from` (`the title after one substitution` `the title`)

§§ `2 -- what the substitution reaches`

-- s 2: "in any written law OR IN ANY OTHER DOCUMENT". Read literally the substitution is not confined to laws or government papers.
-- (Whether a court would confine "any other document" to official documents is not answered by the text; not modelled.)
DECLARE Document IS ONE OF
    `a written law`
    `a government form`
    `a private contract`
    `a private letter`

GIVEN `the document` IS A Document, `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substitution is made in` IF
    `is an old title in the Schedule` `the title`

§§ `3 -- who may add to or amend the Schedule`

-- s 3(1): "The appropriate Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, at any time add to or amend the Schedule."
-- (2): "'appropriate Minister', in relation to any title or name of office, means the Minister charged with the responsibility for the
-- department to which the title or name of office relates."
GIVEN `charged with the department the title relates to` IS A BOOLEAN, `by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may add to or amend the Schedule for that title` IF
    `charged with the department the title relates to` AND `by notification in the Gazette`
